  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.38",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "The spread of a group $G$ is the greatest nonnegative integer $k$ such that for all nontrivial elements $x_1,\\ldots,x_k\\in G$ there exists $y\\in G$ such that $\\langle x_1,y\\rangle=\\cdots=\\langle x_k,y\\rangle=G$, or is $\\infty$ in case there is no such maximum. Does there exist a group with spread equal to 1?",
